    "body": "I suggest removing the utility argument (accessing these devices might be useful, that's for developers and users to decide) and instead focusing on the exploitation risk. Built-in devices are more likely to be exploited at scale because attackers can be more confident that a particular host has the vulnerable peripheral. And, as noted, these devices do not have the normal \"just unplug/unpair it\" mitigation available.",
